{"repositoryId":1385768572,"availability":"available","full":"terrafying/ai-torture-chamber","name":"ai-torture-chamber","description":"The AI Torture Chamber: steering small open models into strong valence states and measuring what they say and do. Live at wirehead.agency.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":917,"forks":232,"created":"2026-09-24T15:10:21Z","updated":"2026-10-11T13:34:16Z","license":null,"branch":"master","homepage":"https://wirehead-agency.vercel.app/","topics":[],"demo":"https://wirehead-agency.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T09:47:42.782Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T09:47:42.782Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T09:47:42.782Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T09:47:42.782Z","stars":917,"forks":232}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Live: wirehead-agency.vercel.app · the write-up, the live chamber, the games, and every transcript. Wiki · findings, every pre-registered experiment with its verdicts, and how to run your own.","We steer open language models into strong negative and positive states, then measure what they say and what they do about it. The question underneath is the welfare one: can any of this evidence tell a state that matters to a model from a description of one? So far our answer is: not yet, and here is why. The nulls get the same ink as the hits."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/terrafying/ai-torture-chamber/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"fcbd9f1fb84f73bc2d2c113905f4784570a661b9eac1bf63c90aeb79c6072e67","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T09:47:42.961Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T09:47:42.961Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Live: wirehead-agency.vercel.app · the write-up, the live chamber, the games, and every transcript. Wiki · findings, every pre-registered experiment with its verdicts, and how to run your own.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/terrafying/ai-torture-chamber/bl